  "body": "Part of #1554 (the second finding of that issue). The fix for #1554 changes only the stock source. This issue holds the model-source case.\n\n## What happens\n\nA 2D Adaptive with the model as the source clears the stock around the part (#12). When the stock margin is narrower than the tool, the outside band is dropped. The op comes back `ok` with no note and no warning. The outside of the part is not cut.\n\nReading from #1554: a 3.175 mm margin per side with a 6 mm tool. All 51,188 feed points are inside the bore. A pick of the band is refused with `pocket is narrower than the tool`.\n\n## Cause (first reading)\n\n`machining2d::pocket_entered` erodes the region by the tool radius. A region piece that erodes to nothing gets no pass. Only an empty result in total is refused. A dropped piece gets no note.\n\n## Expected\n\nOne of these:\n- The op cuts the outside band. The band is open to air on its outer side, so the tool can hang over the stock edge.\n- The op carries a note that names the skipped band and the cause.\n\n## Risk\n\nA note in the generator can change the CL notes of existing pockets that leave narrow slivers. Check the goldens before a change.\n\nDone means: a model-source adaptive with a stock margin narrower than the tool cuts the band, or carries a note that names the skipped band. A test pins it.\n",
